# Airship Simulation Project Structure

## Core Components

### Entry Points
- [main.py](mdc:main.py) - Main entry point
  - Handles simulation execution
  - Manages logging setup
  - Controls simulation modes (BLF/NMPC)
  - Configures trajectory types

### Simulation Modules
- [simulation/](mdc:simulation/) - Core simulation logic
  - Contains simulation execution code
  - Handles trajectory generation
  - Implements control algorithms

### Testing
- [test/](mdc:test/) - Test suite
- [test_desired_trajectory.py](mdc:test_desired_trajectory.py) - Trajectory testing

### Configuration
- [config/](mdc:config/) - Configuration files
- [settings.yaml](mdc:settings.yaml) - Global settings

### Development
- [notebook.ipynb](mdc:notebook.ipynb) - Development and analysis notebook

## Project Organization
- `airship/` - Airship-specific implementations
- `absolute/` - Absolute path utilities
- `logs/` - Runtime logs
- `.cursor/` - Cursor IDE configuration
- `.github/` - GitHub workflows and templates

## Key Features
- Dual controller support (BLF and NMPC)
- Multiple trajectory types
- Comprehensive logging system
- Test suite
- Development notebook for analysis
- Configuration management

## Development Guidelines
1. Use the logging system for debugging
2. Follow the established project structure
3. Add tests for new features
4. Document changes in the notebook